eliezer (0.3.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Add a command line client to the eliezer binary (ls, ps, load, unload, status, run, show,
    help) in the style of ollama and lms; it talks to the running service over HTTP and uses
    --host, --key-file, --json and exit codes 0/1/2/3.
  * Calculate the VRAM requirement per architecture type and schedule loading, eviction,
    pinning, batching and idle handling via a state machine with a clock trait.
  * Measure GPU usage uniformly via a trait (NVML, sysfs, nvidia-smi,
    rocm-smi) with vendor detection, timeout and fallback to bookkeeping.
  * Add backend trait, fake-backend and supervisor task without a real runtime.
  * Provide management API, OpenAI and Anthropic interface with
    unbuffered SSE, authentication and a uniform error format.
  * Integrate supervisor, key file (0600) and GPU measurement into the
    service program; runtimes follow with M4.
  * Verify the model list in the contract test against a real LM Studio response.
  * Add the /v1/completions, /v1/embeddings and /v1/images/generations endpoints and
    report queue, queue length and last use per model in /api/v1/status.
  * Apply a changed configuration and key file on SIGHUP: add and remove models,
    unload removed ones when idle, keep loaded models.
  * Add the embedded llama.cpp runtime (feature rocm, vulkan, cuda or cpu): chat with streaming,
    parallel sequences, prompt-prefix reuse, stop sequences, JSON-schema output, embeddings, the
    models' own Jinja chat templates and parsing of reasoning and tool calls (Qwen, Harmony, Gemma 4).
  * Add `eliezer --import DIR` with `server.run_user` and `server.run_group`: move GGUF models into
    the model store, hand them to the service account and enter them into the validated
    configuration (language and embedding models; image models are only noted).
  * Identify the service with a Server header and make the command line client refuse other
    programs on the port (LM Studio listens on 1234 as well).
  * Fix the systemd unit for a state directory or model store that is a symbolic link, a mount or
    under /home: drop StateDirectory= (systemd refuses a link there), create /var/lib/eliezer in the
    package, make /home read-only instead of hidden.
  * Build a Debian package with cargo-deb (scripts/build-deb.sh): service, systemd unit,
    default configuration, system user; checked in a clean container (tests/deb).
  * Test the documented cases over HTTP, including chat/image alternation, request
    cancellation, GPU measurement failures and an end-to-end configuration reload.

 -- Jörg Bernau <Joerg.Bernau@web.de>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200

eliezer (0.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Create the Rust workspace with five crates and GPL-3.0-only license.
  * Check TOML configurations strictly, with line and field information.
  * Restrict model paths, including symlinks, to the central store.
  * Add CLI, readiness endpoint, logging and signal handling.
  * Set up Linux CI, systemd unit and container build with Rust 1.88.
  * Also check the container build in GitHub CI (image build without push).
  * Provide Compose variants for bind mount, model volume and GPU devices.
  * Document installation and permissions in INSTALL.MD and checks under tests/m2.

 -- Jörg Bernau <Joerg.Bernau@web.de>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:55:32 +0200

eliezer (0.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Complete M1 as a feasibility study on AMD Radeon RX 7900 XTX.
  * Review current runtime sources and document missing AMD features
    of mistral.rs and Candle; confirm llama.cpp with ROCm as a fallback.
  * Demonstrate model loading, token output, two sequences and reloading;
    document the remaining cold VRAM residue and the restart path.
  * Build stable-diffusion.cpp with HIP and test Qwen Image 2.1 over HTTP.
  * Test chat-image-chat directly and with llama-swap; continue with the custom build.
  * Bundle test programs, guides and measurement logs under tests/.
  * Document minimum hardware, permissions, model store and Compose requirements.

 -- Jörg Bernau <Joerg.Bernau@web.de>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:29:30 +0200
